  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO \nCOUNTIES...\n\n...Updated Aviation, Marine, and Beaches discussions...\n\nThis afternoon...The marine layer remains about 1500 feet deep with \na strong inversion so low clouds are persisting at the immediate \ncoast. Low clouds will likely begin to spread inland in the late \nafternoon. Temperatures are mostly within a few degrees of what they \nwere 24 hours ago. A closed upper low to the southwest is enabling \nsome high clouds to move into SoCal from the south in the southerly \nflow aloft.\n\nHigh temperatures today will range from the lower to mid 70s near \nthe coast to the mid 80s to mid 90s in the Inland Empire with 106 to \n110 for the lower deserts. High temperatures inland will rise \nslightly for tomorrow and Saturday. In the coastal areas, \ntemperatures will be within a few degrees each day. Through \nSaturday, high temperatures will generally range from a few degrees \nabove average near the coast to 5 to 10 degrees above average for \nthe mountains and deserts. Moderate HeatRisk will continue for the \ndeserts into next week with the greatest coverage of moderate \nHeatRisk for the Inland Empire on Friday.\n\nThe weak upper low centered about 200 miles off the coast of central \nBaja will continue to push moisture from northern Baja into SoCal \nover the next 24-48 hours as it drifts slowly westward.\nEnough mid-level moisture could spread into the region on Friday for \nthere to be small chances for showers over the mountains in the \nafternoon. The increasing moisture aloft will likely inhibit the \nradiation cooling overnight so that low temperatures will remain \nabove seasonal averages, and some locations could experience record \nhigh minimum temperatures.\n\nHigh temperatures for the mountains and deserts will remain around 4 \nto 8 degrees above average through next Wednesday. For the coast and \nvalleys, high temperatures will cool a few degrees from Sunday \nthrough Wednesday, cooling from within a few degrees of average on \nSunday to a few degrees below average on Wednesday. High \ntemperatures on Sunday will range from the lower to mid 70s near the \ncoast to the mid 80s to mid 90s for the Inland Empire with 108 to \n112 for the lower deserts. Moderate HeatRisk will continue for the \ndeserts through next Wednesday. Night and morning coastal low clouds \nwill spread inland into the western valleys at times.",
